## **Common Anti-Patterns to Avoid**

```tsx
// ❌ DON'T: Use fixed height with object-cover
<div className="relative w-full h-[448px] rounded-t-2xl overflow-hidden">
  <Image
    className="w-full h-full object-cover"
    {/* This crops images */}
  />
</div>

// ❌ DON'T: Use object-cover for images that must be fully visible
<Image
  className="w-full h-full object-cover"
  {/* This will crop important content */}
/>

// ❌ DON'T: Mix fixed height container with object-contain
<div className="relative w-full h-[448px]">
  <Image
    className="w-full h-auto object-contain"
    {/* Container height conflicts with image sizing */}
  />
</div>
```

## **Troubleshooting**

### **Image Still Getting Cropped?**
1. Check container height: Must be `h-auto`, not fixed height (`h-[XXXpx]`)
2. Check image class: Must use `object-contain`, not `object-cover`
3. Check image dimensions: Use `w-full h-auto`, not `w-full h-full`
4. Verify overflow: Container should have `overflow-hidden` for rounded corners

### **Image Too Small?**
- Ensure `width` and `height` props are set appropriately (e.g., `width={800} height={600}`)
- Check if container has sufficient width (`w-full`)
- Verify no conflicting CSS is overriding the styles

### **Image Not Centered?**
- Add `flex items-center justify-center` to container if needed
- Use `object-position: center` in style if required

## **Hero Section Mobile Layout — Special Cases (March 2026)**

The homepage hero section (`src/components/HeroSection.tsx`) uses a 4-section split layout. On mobile (`@media (max-width: 767px)`), different sections require different image strategies. All mobile overrides live in `src/app/globals.css` inside the `@media (max-width: 767px)` block.

### **Section 1 (Kerala Image) — Full-Bleed `object-cover`**

**Exception to the general `object-contain` rule**: Section 1 uses `object-cover` on mobile so the image bleeds edge-to-edge with no gaps. A portrait image with `object-contain` on a full-width mobile viewport leaves purple/background gaps on both sides because the image is narrower than the screen.

```css
/* Mobile: full-width bleed, fixed viewport height, cover fills width */
@media (max-width: 767px) {
  .hero-left-panel {
    width: 100%; padding: 0; margin: 0; min-height: 0;
  }
  .hero-left-image {
    width: 100%; height: auto; padding: 0;
    border-radius: 0; box-shadow: none; border: none;
    background: transparent;
  }
  .hero-left-image img {
    border-radius: 0 !important;
    object-fit: cover !important;   /* fills full width — no side gaps */
    width: 100% !important;
    height: 30vh !important;        /* viewport-relative height; tune to show more/less */
    max-height: none !important;
  }
}
```

**Key decisions**:
- `object-fit: cover` — fills viewport width; slight top/bottom crop is acceptable for this decorative landscape image.
- `height: 30vh` — shows a generous portion of the image. Increase to show more vertically (more crop on sides); decrease to show less.
- Container has `padding: 0`, `border-radius: 0`, `border: none` to ensure true edge-to-edge bleed.
- Desktop (768px+) still uses `object-contain` with `height: 100%` so the full image is visible in the fixed-height panel.

### **Section 3 (Our Mission Card) — Text Overlay on Image**

The mission card has a background image (Unite India logo) with "About" / "Our Mission" text that must sit **on top of** the image, not overflow below it.

```css
@media (max-width: 767px) {
  .hero-bottom-card-mission {
    min-height: 150px;
    overflow: hidden;
    position: relative;
  }

  /* Stronger gradient so white text is readable over the image */
  .hero-bottom-card-mission .hero-mission-overlay {
    background: linear-gradient(to top, rgba(0,0,0,0.55) 0%, rgba(0,0,0,0.2) 40%, transparent 100%);
  }

  /* Absolute positioning keeps text inside the card, overlaying the image */
  .hero-bottom-card-mission .hero-mission-content {
    margin-top: 0;
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 0.5rem;
    left: 0; right: 0;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.75rem;
  }

  /* Smaller text to fit within the card on small screens */
  .hero-bottom-card-mission .hero-card-label {
    font-size: 0.625rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.125rem;
  }
  .hero-bottom-card-mission .hero-card-title {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
  }

  /* Contain the Unite India logo so it's fully visible (not cropped on right) */
  .hero-bottom-card-mission .hero-mission-bg img {
    object-fit: contain !important;
    object-position: center center !important;
  }
}
```

**Key decisions**:
- `position: absolute; bottom: 0.5rem` on `.hero-mission-content` — anchors text to bottom of card, overlaying the image.
- `min-height: 150px` — enough room for image + text overlay.
- Stronger gradient overlay (`rgba(0,0,0,0.55)`) at the bottom ensures white text readability.
- Smaller font sizes (label: 0.625rem, title: 0.8125rem) prevent text overflow on narrow screens.
- Mission bg image uses `object-contain` (unlike Section 1) because the Unite India logo must be fully visible.

